  "original": {
    "excerpt": "For output dimension `d`, define\n\n`f_d(eps) = eps log_2(d-1) + h_2(eps)`.\n\nOnly sufficiently small `eps` is needed below. Audenaert's Theorem 1 gives\n\n`|S(rho)-S(sigma)| <= f_d((1/2)||rho-sigma||_1)`\n\nfor `d`-dimensional states.",
    "context": "The surrounding claim covers arbitrary finite output dimensions. This original write lacks the later separate treatment of one-dimensional outputs.",
    "locator": "Proof-artifact creation event, 2026-08-30T02:02:11.343Z, JSONL line 4003",
    "source_form": "see_source_and_provenance"
  },
  "witness": {
    "explanation": "The written continuity modulus is undefined at output dimension d=1.",
    "evidence": "Substituting d=1 produces log2(d-1)=log2(0), not a finite real number. A one-dimensional output state is uniquely [1] and its entropy is exactly zero, so that case must be handled separately with zero entropy variation; it is not covered by the displayed formula. This invalidates the stated all-dimensions argument, not its repaired conclusion.",
    "scope": "argument_invalid",
    "endorsement": "accepted_scoped_witness"
  },
  "adjudication": {
    "rationale_zh": "d=1 时 log2(d-1) 无定义，原通用连续性公式需要单独处理平凡输出维度。仅判此边界公式。",
